{"isConditionalPasskeysEnabled() returns false when user == null, but conditional passkey UI is needed on the initial login screen before a user is identified. In authenticate(), the call isConditionalPasskeysEnabled(context.getUser()) with context.getUser() == null for first-time anonymous logins causes webauthnAuth.fillContextForm(context) to never execute, omitting WebAuthn conditional UI attributes and breaking the passkey flow for anonymous login attempts": 0.7837942242622375, "fillContextForm() uses shouldShowWebAuthnAuthenticators(context) to decide whether the user is identified, which breaks subclasses like WebAuthnConditionalUIAuthenticator that override shouldShowWebAuthnAuthenticators() to always return false. This causes IS_USER_IDENTIFIED to be set to false and skips building ALLOWED_AUTHENTICATORS, starting an identifier-less WebAuthn ceremony instead of a user-specific one, preventing users with non-resident credentials from authenticating because they need the server-provided allow-list": 0.6434400081634521}